          <th style="padding: 12px; text-align: left;">Price / Carat</th>
        </tr>
        <tr style="background: #fdfaf5;"><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;"><strong>Columbia</strong></td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">The global benchmark</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Rich, warm, vivid green</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">₹8,000 – ₹10,00,000+</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;"><strong>Swat / Panjshir</strong></td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Bright &amp; lively</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Bright green with visible natural texture</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">₹3,000 – ₹3,00,000+</td></tr>
        <tr style="background: #fdfaf5;"><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;"><strong>Zambia</strong></td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Strong &amp; durable</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Forest to bluish-green</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">₹2,500 – ₹5,00,000+</td></tr>
        <tr><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;"><strong>Russia</strong></td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Cool &amp; structured</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Bluish to grey-green</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">₹4,00,000+</td></tr>
        <tr style="background: #fdfaf5;"><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;"><strong>Brazil</strong></td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Soft &amp; approachable</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">Light to medium green</td><td style="padding: 12px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">₹1,500 – ₹1,50,000+</td></tr>
      </table>
      <p style="margin-top: 16px;">Beyond origin, price is shaped by colour vibrancy, saturation, transparency, treatment level, clarity balance, cut quality, and structural stability. With Emerald, a smaller stone with vivid life and natural balance will almost always outperform a larger one that looks flat, dull, or overly treated.</p>
      <div style="background: #fdfaf5; padding: 20px; border-left: 4px solid var(--color-gold); margin-top: 20px;">
        <p style="margin:0;"><strong>Ideal Weight:</strong> 2–7 carats, depending on the horoscope and Mercury’s strength.</p>
        <p style="margin:8px 0 0;"><strong>Best Metal:</strong> Gold, traditionally. Silver only when astrologically advised.</p>
      </div>
    {%- when 'blue-sapphire' -%}
      <p>Origin is one of the most significant factors in a Blue Sapphire's value. Two stones that look similar can differ enormously in price based on where they came from — and that origin should always be disclosed and lab-verified for premium pieces.</p>
